Actually, I hoped that a source diver would provide us with the right 
figures.  But this seems to be a discussion only between you and me, so 
I'll try to provide some numbers.  IIRC, a monster does not appear, 
unless its level is not higher than the average of your level and the 
dungeon level.  I'll assume in the following that the castle is at level 25.

Arch liches are level 25.  So you are safe not to encounter an arch 
lich, if your level is below 25.  I was actually assuming that you are 
looking for MR and have not even reached the level to do the quest; the 
number that I gave was level 12.  So it is with certainty that you won't 
meet an arch lich at the castle.

Master liches are level 17.  So the first level they can appear on for a 
12th level character is level 22.  So they *are* possible at the castle 
(and you would have to be level 8 to avoid them with certainty, which is 
rather unlikely).  I don't know anything about the probability of first 
arrivals, but I seem to remember that an "early" master lich will be 
weaker that a "late" one and that there is a range of levels where the 
appearance probability is maximum.  I suppose, this maximum has not been 
reached at the castle yet, therefore the relatively small probability of 
their appearance there (if you are still at level 12).

